ly two  of them with their hands behind their  backs those being paristan and saiyu who  ended up being the two to betray the  organization it's subtle so subtle that  it almost makes you think that you are  the crazy one until togashi comes clean  and eventually does reveal the answer in  this case the cover and the author's  note are more brazen than any that have  come before it but one question i do  have is regarding the three flowers for  the illumi as he soaked her idea to work  this would imply that hisoka is  connected to three deaths but  deciphering the third is not necessarily  that straightforward karapika was the  clear cause of death foo of agin and i  would say the same for pakunoda but in  the past hisoka did defeat another troop  member who held the number 4 spot and  while it was never explicitly stated  that he killed that member i don't  really see many other outcomes in which  that battle would have concluded so that  could be our three dead troop members  shall not cortopia and the former number  four all slain by the bungalicious hand  of hisoka the other way you could  interpret this cover is a reference not  to the past but to the future this could  be telling us who hisoka is going to  kill which would make sense with the  lips of the volume warning us about  potential spoilers and if you were to go  by who the flowers were closest to that  would be finks kalato and either shizuku  or franklin that's the simplest way to  look at it anyway i suppose you could  also analyze the flowers by color or  however you like but that's the general  idea that they are there and they mean  things either way the flowers represent  dead troop members or they foreshadow  future deaths of troop members and  whatever the case may be they are  connected to illumi a man who has  absolutely no reason to be involved in  such connections but if this is hisoka  then firstly this is sinister half and  secondly it makes all the sense in the  world but i'd also like to bring up a  scene in the mangrove villami's  conversation with mizeistom after the  troop decide to split up illimi and  kalato get rather hilariously caught  almost immediately after which point  illumi requests a cell with a shower now  this is i will admit some glorious  overthinking i warn you but illumi has  never been the type of person to be  overly conscious of his own cleanliness  i mean the dude even slept in a hole  that one time on the other hand frequent  bathing is practically another hisoka  motif such as when we dwell on him  showering at heaven's arena but we do  also intrude on him bathing a greed  island he may be a sick twisted  degenerate thirsty battle clown but at  least he's a clean clown i'll grant that  this is probably one of the most  outlandish connections of the video but  at the same time illemi's words once  again they're just very out of character  illumi is not the kind of person who  wastes words requesting a room with a  shower that he doesn't need and during  this conversation illumi also gives up  the information that the entirety of the  phantom trooper aboard the ship which is  information that he volunteers  volunteers being a very key word because  illumi does not volunteer especially if  it's relevant to his current job i  really cannot emphasize enough just how  flippant and reckless illumi is being on  these pages and how it is very unlike  the illumi that we know now let's get  into some of the issues with this theory  because carlito has been brought up a  couple of times and he does present a  potential problem hisoka might be able  to fool the troop into thinking that  he's illimi but kalito as a brother of  illemi should probably know better i  mean yeah they're quite a few years  apart they probably don't spend a ton of  time together but in theory karlito  should probably be able to recognize  that philome is acting slightly  naughtily so to account for that we may  need to get a little bit more convoluted  we either need to suggest that carlato  has no idea whatsoever an incident is  just kind of meh writing or that kalato  has no strong connection to illumi  despite their brotherliness or that  kalato does know and he is in on the  clever ruse it's not too far out of the  realm of possibility because carlito has  no real loyalty to the troop he's only  there for the very vague mission of  getting his brother back the meaning of  which is a gigantic question in and of  itself and in fact i have a whole video  discussing that issue which i do  recommend checking out but all hisoka  really needs to do is promise to assist  kalato just as he has done in the past  notably would say karapika during york  new city but this does require that  extra layer of thought and if this were  any other series i wouldn't even bother  to go that far but togashi does engage  in these kind of complex cerebral  scenarios so for better or worse nothing  is ever off the table in hunter hunter  and even with it on the table the  evidence is reaching a critical mass  tagashi has dripped in enough subtle  hints to paint a beautifully  foreshadowed picture without completely  giving away the game illumi speaks like  hisoka his design incorporates one of  hisoka's trademarks hisoka does have the  technical ability to make this a reality  and togashi is heavily suggesting that  there is something very off about illumi  in regards to the author's notes and  cover of volume 36 at this point i would  be much more surprised if this actually  was illumi although that's not off the  table either there could exist a  situation where two things are true and  dilemmy is working with hisoka whilst  hisoka is impersonating enemy and  they're both just running around and  doing stupid clown things there's  definitely a lot of different ways this  could go but the one piece of certainty  we have is that this illumi is not what  he seems and i am convinced that this is  actually hisoka in disguise but if you'd  like to examine another fun hunt  hunter's theory then i have another  video that details the history and logic  behind the feitan is actually a zoldic  theory i know it sounds pretty absurd  but hey so did this video and there's a  good deal of substance to it so i look  forward to seeing you there
 

